# Forklift API Webhooks

> Analyzed from commit: `baf9c7bcc307ed9358ad59886a5536366a050012` on 2026-09-17
> Source paths: `pkg/forklift-api/webhooks/`, `pkg/forklift-api/api.go`

## Package Purpose

The forklift-api process runs Kubernetes admission webhooks over TLS. It validates and mutates Forklift CRDs (Plans, Migrations, Providers) and their associated Secrets before they are persisted to etcd. Webhooks enforce authorization, connection testing, storage compatibility, and default field population.

---

## Server Setup

```
pkg/forklift-api/api.go  →  ForkliftApi.Execute()
  ├── goroutine: serveServices()   → :8444 (REST services, see rest-api.mdc)
  └── serveWebhooks()              → :8443 (admission webhooks)
```

| Setting | Value |
|---------|-------|
| Port | 8443 |
| TLS certs | `API_TLS_CERTIFICATE`, `API_TLS_KEY` env vars |
| Framework | Plain `net/http.ServeMux` |
| API version | `admission/v1beta1` (backwards-compatible with v1) |

